  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily and Mia have a small library. It is in the living room. They have a bookcase and ten books. \"Our library is open!\" says Lily. Grandma comes with her handbag. \"Hello, girls!\" says Grandma. \"Can I read a book?\" \"Yes, please,\" says Mia. \"Sit in the armchair, Grandma.\" Grandma sits in the armchair.",
      "Mia gives her a book about animals. Grandma looks at the book. \"I can't read it,\" says Grandma. \"Where are my glasses?\" She looks in her handbag. She looks on the table. Mia looks under the armchair. Lily looks behind the bookcase. Pip jumps on Grandma's leg. He looks at her head. \"Woof!\" says Pip.",
      "Lily looks at Grandma's head. \"Grandma, your glasses are there!\" Grandma puts her hand on her head. \"Oh, here they are!\" Grandma smiles. \"Thank you, Pip!\" Now she can read the book. \"Is the library good?\" asks Mia. \"It is very good,\" says Grandma. Pip sits on her leg."
    ],
    "summary": "Lily and Mia have a small library at home. Grandma cannot find her glasses, but Pip finds them on her head.",
